// The typed IR (`ctxc ir`): a loop gets an id only if an inner loop's jump leaves or repeats
// it; a labeled jump to the innermost loop is plain.
// The IR is the program's and std's, with ids that change when std does: what is stated is
// the part the test is about, with `{n}` for the ids.
//# $ ctxc ir {std} -- main0.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# stdout has:
//| (continue 1)
//# stdout has:
//| (break 2)
//# stdout has:
//| (break)
//# stdout has:
//|
//|     } 1)
//|   } 2)
